==French==

===Pronunciation===
* {{fr-IPA}}
* {{audio|fr|Fr-puis.ogg|audio}}
* {{homophones|fr|puits|puy}}
* {{rhymes|fr|ɥi|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|fr|VL.|*postius}}, a comparative of {{der|fr|la|post||after}}.<ref>{{cite-book|fr|last=Picoche|first=Jacqueline|coauthors=Jean-Claude Rolland|title=Dictionnaire étymologique du français|year=2009|publisher=Dictionnaires Le Robert|location=Paris}}</ref> Compare {{cog|pt|pois}}, {{cog|es|pues}}, {{cog|it|poi}}, and {{cog|ro|apoi}} (archaic {{m|ro|păi}}).

====Adverb====
{{fr-adv}}

# [[then]]; [[after]]; [[next]]

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|fr|et puis quoi encore}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|fr|depuis}}

====Conjunction====
{{head|fr|conjunction}}

# [[and]]

===Etymology 2===
{{inh+|fr|VL.|*posseō}}, alteration of earlier {{m|VL.|possō}}, a regularization of {{inh|fr|la|possum}}. Compare {{cog|roa-oca|puix}}.

====Verb====
{{head|fr|verb form}}

# {{lb|fr|archaic|or|literary}} {{inflection of|fr|pouvoir||1|s|pres|indc}}
#* {{quote-book|fr|year=1862|author=w:Victor Hugo|title=Les Misérables, Tome I - FANTINE|publisher=Ebooks libres et gratuits|page=135
|passage=—Dans tous les cas, ce que je '''puis''' dire, c’est que, s’il a eu toutes ces idées, il n’en a rien marqué, même pour moi|t=In any case, all I '''can''' say is that, if that is what he thought, he showed nothing of it, not even to me}}
#* {{quote-book|fr|year=2000|author=w:Jean-François Parot|title=L'énigme des Blancs-Manteaux|publisher=JC Lattès|year_published=2012|page=24
|passage=—Monsieur, dit-il, je vous salue et vous serais obligé de m'indiquer si je '''puis''' être reçu par M. de Sartine.|t=‘Sir,’ he said, ‘I bid you good-day, and would be obliged if you could tell me whether I '''might''' be received by M. Sartine.’}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Now generally used only in the highly formal inverted question form (''puis-je'' "may I"). A common alternative is ''Est-ce que je peux'' or more simply in a colloquial context: ''Je peux'' or ''J'peux'' (pronounced /ʃpø/).

